---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const normalizeDefectsResult = await normalizeDefects(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const traceExposureResult = await traceExposure(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, normalizeDefectsResult.accepted);
const compareCausesResult = await compareCauses(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, traceExposureResult.accepted);
const planCorrectionResult = await planCorrection(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, compareCausesResult.accepted);
const verifyEffectivenessResult = await verifyEffectiveness(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, planCorrectionResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { normalizeDefects: normalizeDefectsResult, traceExposure: traceExposureResult, compareCauses: compareCausesResult, planCorrection: planCorrectionResult, verifyEffectiveness: verifyEffectivenessResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...normalizeDefectsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...traceExposureResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...compareCausesResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...planCorrectionResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...verifyEffectivenessResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...normalizeDefectsResult.checks, ...traceExposureResult.checks, ...compareCausesResult.checks, ...planCorrectionResult.checks, ...verifyEffectivenessResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — A lot was reworked under a different process: preserve both histories in exposure tracing. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (preserve both histories in exposure tracing.) through the existing stage result for DefectObservation; preserve exact source/version and the prior DefectObservation, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — Inspection methods changed: avoid treating changed detection rates as changed defect rates. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (avoid treating changed detection rates as changed defect rates.) through the existing stage result for DefectObservation; preserve exact source/version and the prior DefectObservation, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — An operator is named in a report: do not infer blame from correlation. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (do not infer blame from correlation.) through the existing stage result for DefectObservation; preserve exact source/version and the prior DefectObservation, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — A hold is lifted for only part of a lot: maintain unit-level release scope. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (maintain unit-level release scope.) through the existing stage result for DefectObservation; preserve exact source/version and the prior DefectObservation, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — A defect recurs after closure: reopen the causal claim and effectiveness test. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (reopen the causal claim and effectiveness test.) through the existing stage result for DefectObservation; preserve exact source/version and the prior DefectObservation, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, normalizeDefects: normalizeDefectsResult, traceExposure: traceExposureResult, compareCauses: compareCausesResult, planCorrection: planCorrectionResult, verifyEffectiveness: verifyEffectivenessResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
